<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a>–<a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spanish Civil War was fought between the Second Spanish Republic and the Nationalist rebels led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-franco">Francisco Franco</a>, who rose in July 1936. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> aided the Nationalists and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> the Republic. The Basque autonomous government fell in 1937, and the Nationalist victory in 1939 began Franco's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-civil-war.jpg" alt="Spanish Civil War" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%98%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_11_%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%B2_%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%8E_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B4_%D0%91%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%87%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5._1937-edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>During the <b>Spanish Civil War</b> and the Second World War the mountain paths served as routes for refugees, escapers and smugglers.</blockquote><a href="/empire/andorra">Andorra · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Mussolini’s regime conquered Ethiopia in 1935–1936, using poison gas, sent forces to the <b>Spanish Civil War</b> and occupied Albania in 1939.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Condor Legion fought for Franco in the <b>Spanish Civil War</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>This classical era, the golden age of anarchism, lasted until the end of the <b>Spanish Civil War</b>.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/anarchism">Anarchism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>Francoist Spain arose from the <b>Spanish Civil War</b> of 1936–1939 as a compromise between Falangism and clerical authoritarianism, and whether Franco’s dictatorship was fascist is debated.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/fascism">Fascism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>In the <b>Spanish Civil War</b> it became one of the main anarchist anthems, together with &quot;Hijos del Pueblo&quot;, and was often featured in the CNT's propaganda films.</blockquote><a href="/songs/a-las-barricadas">A las Barricadas</a></li></ul></section>
